meta {
  name: 4 Check what a block would strand
  type: http
  seq: 4
}
get {
  url: {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/calendar/blocks/{{providerEmail}}/conflicts?startUtc=2026-09-21T00:00:00Z&endUtc=2026-09-24T00:00:00Z
}
params:query {
  startUtc: 2026-09-21T00:00:00Z
  endUtc: 2026-09-24T00:00:00Z
}
docs {
  The live sessions a proposed range would strand, read **before** creating the block — so the cost is
  visible in advance rather than discovered from a refusal.

  Cancelled and completed sessions are excluded: neither is something a block can strand. Overlap, not
  containment — a session that begins before the range and runs into it is just as stranded as one wholly
  inside it. Half-open on both sides, so a session ending exactly as the range opens is untouched.

  Owner-only: it returns whole appointments, which carry the counterparty's email address.

  `400` when the range does not end after it starts.
}
